      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "About the session",
          "_key": "k0013"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0014",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Christine Sheller, a seasoned design professional and teacher, is leading an engaging discussion focused on the critical role of research in informing design across various disciplines. Held Thursday, June 26, from 10:45-11:45 am, this session is designed to provide attendees with a thorough understanding of practical discovery methods, empowering designers to create impactful, user-centric solutions. The content covers the entire spectrum, from initial discovery through ideation.",
          "_key": "k0015"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0016",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "Participants will gain insights into popular research methodologies used in design. The session not only outlines these methodologies but also explores their practical applications.",
          "_key": "k0017"
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "_type": "block",
      "style": "normal"
    },
    {
      "_key": "k0018",
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The Audience Will Learn:",
          "_key": "k0019"
